// seeds.memql
//
// The certification ladder's values (epic memql#5408, issue #5409).
//
// ONE GLOBAL SEED, and its NAME is its row id: a global seed with no `id` in
// its body takes the seed's name, so `seed ladderPolicy primary` materializes
// v1:authoring:ladderPolicy:primary through createLadderPolicy. Every read
// (ladderPolicyCurrent) pins that literal id.
//
// REFRESHED ON EVERY BOOT. The seed materializer re-asserts every global seed
// on every node at startup, and the fields a seed declares win, so these
// numbers are the ones the ladder applies after any restart -- the same
// refresh the cluster singletons get, without a gate of their own. A write
// that does not change a value is skipped (seedRowIsCurrent), so an unchanged
// seed costs one read per node per boot and appends no version.
//
// THE SAME NUMBERS LIVE IN GO EXACTLY ONCE, as
// component/work.DefaultLadderPolicy(), and only for a row that is absent or
// unreadable. Changing a value here changes the ladder; changing it there
// changes nothing while this row exists.

/// The certification ladder's values: m = 5 shadow matches across k = 2 distinct bindings per
/// free parameter propose a promotion to canary; 5 clean canary replays make a procedure trusted;
/// 2 failed replays, or 1 replay whose preconditions proved insufficient, demote it to shadow; 30
/// days without a replay retire it.
seed ladderPolicy primary {
  shadowMatches:         5
  distinctBindings:      2
  canaryMatches:         5
  failuresToDemote:      2
  insufficientToDemote:  1
  retireAfterDays:       30
}
